    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65151" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαστῑγο-φόρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>scourge-bearing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπηρέται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					35.1
				</span></i>
			; epith. of Ajax, Arg.<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst., <i>policeman</i>, esp. at the Games, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				40
			</span></i>: generally, of attendants on officials, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. οἰκονόμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTeb.</u>
					121.58
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				179
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρας μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
					80.4
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>.</div>
